WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.280
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I'm going&nbsp;
to explain an American psychological thriller&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.200
film called “Fractured.” Spoilers&nbsp;
ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.080
Ray Monroe, with his wife Joanne and his daughter&nbsp;
Perri, is driving home from his in-law’s house.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.960
It is the day of thanksgiving. The couple&nbsp;
argues about their relationship ,as Perri&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.680
sits in the backseat listening to music on her&nbsp;
headphones. Joanne begins to cry, knowing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.720
their marriage is at its ending. As they argue,&nbsp;
Perri’s headphones stop working, so the couple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.840
stops arguing and sings songs with Perri to keep&nbsp;
her entertained. Sometime later, Perri has to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.600
to the bathroom. Ray pulls over at a gas station.&nbsp;
Joanne takes Perri to the washroom, as Ray goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.400
to buy batteries for Perri’s headphones,&nbsp;
coffee, and a coke for Joanne. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.720
he is short on money, so he ditches the batteries&nbsp;
and gets two liquor bottles for himself. 
&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.320
Back in the car, he lies to Joanne, telling&nbsp;
her that the store did not have batteries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:03.760
Ray is about to start the car, when Perri notices&nbsp;
that her compact is missing. When they do not find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.240
it in the car, Joanne goes to look for it&nbsp;
in the washroom. Ray gets up to check under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:14.160
Perri’s seat but accidentally drops his coffee.&nbsp;
Perri is outside the car. As Ray is distracted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.200
Perri wanders off to a nearby construction&nbsp;
site. She sees a balloon and goes near it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.720
Just then, a dog comes near her; she starts&nbsp;
calling Ray for help. As Perri retreats, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:30.080
is stuck between the dog and a construction pit.
Ray finally notices the dog, and asks Perri not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.040
to move and slowly tries to advert the dog’s&nbsp;
direction towards himself. Just as Ray throws&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.920
a stone at it, Perri gets scared and falls into&nbsp;
the pit. Ray runs to save her and falls into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.880
the pit as well; he falls unconscious. He wakes&nbsp;
up a few seconds later and sees Joanne running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.280
towards them. Perri lies unconscious beside&nbsp;
him, while Joanne checks her for injuries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:54.640
Ray is still in shock and doesn’t say anything.&nbsp;
Joanne comes to him crying hysterically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.760
but he pushes her aside. Ray closes his eyes,&nbsp;
and when he opens it, everything seems normal. 
&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:06.000
Perri opens her eyes, and he takes a sigh of&nbsp;
relief. However, her arm seems to be fractured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.800
so Ray gently picks Perri and takes her to the&nbsp;
car. Joanne suggests they call an ambulance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.120
but Ray claims to see a hospital nearby.&nbsp;
While they drive to the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:20.480
Ray nearly crashes into another car. Perri lies in&nbsp;
the backseat with Joanne and is in a lot of pain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.200
When the family gets to the hospital, Joanne&nbsp;
and Perri sit in the waiting area as Ray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.000
checks them in. The hospital is crowded, so the&nbsp;
receptionist tells him to wait for their turn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.840
As the three of them wait, Perri whimpers in pain.&nbsp;
Ray goes to the receptionist again and asks to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:41.280
sent earlier than others. However, she just makes&nbsp;
him sign paperwork and asks him to wait. He goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.840
back to his family in the waiting area, where&nbsp;
Joanne apologizes to him for being rude earlier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.960
After a while, the nurse calls Ray’s&nbsp;
name. The family is taken to a room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:55.920
where the nurse notes down required information&nbsp;
about them. The questions start to get intrusive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.560
which annoys the couple. The nurse then asks&nbsp;
them to register Perri as an organ donor, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:06.880
they refuse. Even after being denied, the nurse&nbsp;
pushes the topic, but Ray dismisses her. Another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:12.240
nurse then takes them to a ward. Perri is put into&nbsp;
a hospital bed, and a doctor finally sees her. 
&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.320
He confirms that Perri’s arm is broken&nbsp;
and tells them that she needs a cast.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.520
When the doctor finds out that Perri has also&nbsp;
hit her head, he advises them to do a CT scan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.360
The nurses cast Perri’s arm. She is then put&nbsp;
in a wheelchair and taken to the CT scan lab.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:33.520
It turns out that only one parent can go to the&nbsp;
area at once, so Ray stays outside. Perri tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.640
him that she loves him before they part. Ray&nbsp;
falls asleep while waiting for them. He wakes up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:43.440
in a few hours, and asks the receptionist about&nbsp;
his family, but since the shifts have changed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.600
she doesn’t know anything. She asks him&nbsp;
to wait while she checks the records.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.800
It has been several minutes, but the receptionist&nbsp;
doesn’t say anything. Ray asks her again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.160
this time a little annoyed. She then checks the&nbsp;
morning record, but Perri’s name is not in it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:04.240
Frustrated, Ray asks to see the doctor who checked&nbsp;
Perri, but he has changed shifts too. Agitated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.160
Ray yells at the receptionist and bangs her desk,&nbsp;
so she immediately calls the CT room. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.840
the person from the lab tells her that only&nbsp;
one old woman has come to the lab that day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:19.120
Ray is beyond frustrated; he angrily asks her&nbsp;
about his family, but the receptionist looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.200
at him as if he is crazy. She even blames&nbsp;
him for coming into the wrong hospital.
&nbsp;

00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:28.160
Ray insists that it is not possible, but she&nbsp;
ignores him and starts talking to someone else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:33.040
Worried about his family, Ray runs to the&nbsp;
restricted area of the hospital...only to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:38.160
stopped by the officials there. He informs them&nbsp;
of their visit this morning. The doctor checks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:43.600
the day’s record but sees no patient by the name&nbsp;
of Monroe. Frustrated, Ray looks around and sees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:48.640
the nurse who helped them earlier. The nurse&nbsp;
recognizes Ray. Believing that he has proved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.200
his point, Ray sighs in relief, but the nurse&nbsp;
adds that she doesn’t know anything about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:57.920
daughter or his wife. According to her, Ray&nbsp;
came in for a head injury and was alone. 
&nbsp;

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.760
Agitated, Ray blames the nurse for lying. The&nbsp;
doctor assumes he has a contusion from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:09.680
head injury and offers to treat him. However, Ray&nbsp;
almost attacks the nurse and has to be restrained.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.120
The doctor injects him with sedatives to calm him&nbsp;
down. He is then locked into a room by the guards;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.600
Ray tries to unlock the door, but the drugs&nbsp;
make him hazy. To make the sedative not work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:24.160
he injects himself with an injection he finds&nbsp;
in the cabinets. He then tries to unlock the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:30.080
door again, but it doesn’t work. Hence, he breaks&nbsp;
the glass door and runs out of the room. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.520
before he can escape, people notice him running&nbsp;
away. The security chases him; but Ray somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.720
manages to run out of the hospital and hide in his&nbsp;
car. A police car is right outside the hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:46.000
too. Taking the opportunity, Ray stops the car&nbsp;
and tells the police about Joanne and Perri. 
&nbsp;

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:52.160
The police, suspecting that he is lying, ask&nbsp;
for identifiCTion. After he shows them his ID,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.600
they agree to help him. The receptionist sees Ray&nbsp;
walk into the hospital again, but this time, she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.880
cannot do anything because of the police officers.&nbsp;
She calls the security before assisting them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.440
The guards then let them in. Ray takes&nbsp;
the police to the doctor from earlier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.520
The doctor admits that there can be a mistake&nbsp;
in the records, and Ray demands they be taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:17.600
to the CT lab. The doctor agrees; however, the&nbsp;
guards take them to the third floor; Ray clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:22.480
remembers the CT lab being in the basement.
At the lab, it is clear that Perri was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:27.040
never there. Ray then demands to call doctor&nbsp;
Berthram, who had checked Perri that morning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.480
The staff obliges. Just then, the receptionist&nbsp;
comes in with the paper that Ray had signed this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:38.400
morning. However, it doesn’t prove the presence of&nbsp;
Joanne and Perri. Doctor Berthram finally arrives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.560
and reveals that Ray came to the hospital&nbsp;
alone to get treated for his head injury.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:47.120
The doctor had asked him to do a CT scan,&nbsp;
but he refused, saying that his wife Abby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:52.000
was waiting for him outside. The police officers&nbsp;
get suspicious of Ray because he has told them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.960
that his wife’s name is Joanne; not Abby.&nbsp;
Ray then reveals that Abby is his ex-wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:01.840
who has been dead for years. Helpless, Ray&nbsp;
accuses the hospital of kidnapping his family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:07.280
The security guard suggests they look at the&nbsp;
CCTV camera footage to see if Ray is lying. 
&nbsp;

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.000
The group then watches the footage for the&nbsp;
morning, but Perri and Joanne are in none of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:17.360
Ray claims that it is because of the camera’s&nbsp;
angle. The police officers do not believe Ray’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.880
story anymore. Ray then asks them to go to the&nbsp;
gas station to figure the truth. He even finds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.840
Perri’s scarf near the hospital bed she was in the&nbsp;
morning. He claims that this proves she was here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:32.480
but the police need more evidence than that. The&nbsp;
doctors suspect that Ray is not in a mentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:37.760
stable condition, so they introduce him to a&nbsp;
psychiatrist named Teresa Jacobs. Teresa takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:42.240
Ray to a room and shows him his administration&nbsp;
record, which doesn’t mention Perri or Joanne. 
&nbsp;

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:47.920
Teresa calmly talks to him and inquires about&nbsp;
the incidents of that morning. She also asks him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:53.120
about Abby. Ray then reveals that Abby died eight&nbsp;
years ago in a car accident, and he couldn’t save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:58.800
her because he was drunk. Frustrated, he starts&nbsp;
to cry. Teresa now knows for sure that something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.280
is wrong. She suggests the police go look at&nbsp;
the place the accident occurred this morning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:09.120
According to Teresa, Joanne and Perri might still&nbsp;
be there. The police officers then take Ray and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:14.080
Teresa to the construction site again. They&nbsp;
call for backup to help them with the search.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:18.800
Then they find Perri’s compact on the pit. They&nbsp;
also see a pool of dried blood in the concrete. 
&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:24.240
The police realize that this cannot be Ray’s&nbsp;
blood, because his injury isn’t that bad. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:28.240
missing people and the blood make the officers&nbsp;
realize that the place is a crime scene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:34.240
However, Ray, in turn, blames the police officers&nbsp;
for planting the compact and the blood to falsely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:38.240
accuse Ray. He believes that the police want&nbsp;
to save the hospital for what they have done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:43.840
to Joanne and Perri. Teresa, on the other hand,&nbsp;
tries to calm Ray down and asks him what happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:49.600
to Perri. Ray starts to blabber. Teresa then&nbsp;
asks him if he pushed Perri down the pit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:54.160
This makes Ray go silent. He doesn’t&nbsp;
move and stares into the distance. 
&nbsp;

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:58.480
The police then arrest him on the suspicion of&nbsp;
killing his wife and his daughter. As they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:03.280
about to handcuff him, Ray snaps. He snatches&nbsp;
the officer’s gun and points it at Teresa.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:08.720
Then, he makes them go into the gas station&nbsp;
and locks them there. Taking Teresa’s key card,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:13.600
Ray drives to the hospital in a police&nbsp;
car. He hides the gun and goes inside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:17.920
His plan is to go to the basement, where he&nbsp;
believes that Joanne and Perri are captured.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:22.960
While he is at it, he comes across the maternity&nbsp;
room. The children remind him of the day Abby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:27.120
died. He reminisces of the death which had&nbsp;
killed both Abby and his unborn kid. 
&nbsp;

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:32.640
He somehow manages to get a doctor’s apron&nbsp;
and disguises himself as one. He gets into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:37.360
the elevator and is about to go to the basement,&nbsp;
but the security guard from earlier joins him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.240
He and Ray get into a fight. In the end, Ray&nbsp;
strangles the guard to death and takes his keys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.480
Ray is finally in the basement of&nbsp;
the hospital. As he looks around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:51.280
he finds Perri’s toy in a bin nearby. Sure&nbsp;
that his daughter is somewhere near, he takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:56.000
the gun in his hand and searches for her.
Then, he sees two doctors delivering boxes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:00.880
of human organs somewhere. Ray finally realizes&nbsp;
that Joanne and Perri were brought here to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:05.680
their organs harvested. This explains the nurse&nbsp;
trying to make Perri an organ donor that morning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:11.600
Ray then enters a room, and is horrified to see&nbsp;
several dead bodies with missing organs. He rushes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:15.840
out of the room looking for Perri, and finally&nbsp;
finds her in another room being operated on by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:21.200
surgeons. Joanne is in the corner of the room,&nbsp;
highly sedated. The doctors had drugged her. 
&nbsp;

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:26.880
Ray then holds the surgeons at gunpoint, and&nbsp;
places both Joanne and Perri in a wheelchair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:31.760
But before he can run away, the doctors restrain&nbsp;
him. They are about to inject him with drugs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.600
but Ray manages to free himself by&nbsp;
shooting a device and causing an explosion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:39.600
Ray finally runs out of the room with&nbsp;
both Joanne and Perri in the wheelchair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:44.560
He kills another doctor in the hallway. 
He brings his family out of the hospital&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.560 --> 00:10:49.760
and puts them in the backseat of his car. The&nbsp;
family finally drives away to their home. Perri&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:54.800
tells them that her arm still hurts, so Ray sings&nbsp;
her a song to make her feel better. Just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.040
the camera pans to the back seat, and we see that&nbsp;
the people sitting there are two random people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:03.680
that Ray has kidnapped from the middle of their&nbsp;
surgery. Ray gets flashbacks from the morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:08.480
and we get to know that Perri died when she fell&nbsp;
into the pit. When Ray pushed Joanne, he killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:13.200
her as well. Ray’s mind couldn’t handle the pain&nbsp;
of him being the reason for his family’s death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:18.480
Hence, his mind constructs a new reality in&nbsp;
which both his wife and daughter are still alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:23.280
Ray believes he is rescuing them, but it is&nbsp;
revealed that he has kidnapped a random patient&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:27.840
from surgery. Joanne and Perri’s dead bodies were&nbsp;
inside the trunk of his car the whole time. 
&nbsp;

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:32.720
The movie ends as Ray hallucinates Joanne&nbsp;
telling him to take them home. And that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:36.400
the heartbreaking ending of the movie! 
